"notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental funds from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); balance used for roll-forward is fund balance (64,035 to 92,215), which differs from governmental cash assets (94,772) by liabilities of 2,557. Business-type from the proprietary funds statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p7): receipts = sales + misc + interest; disbursements = operating expenses + capital outlay + debt principal and interest (nonoperating lines, which are cash disbursements); transfers out 10,000 (net position roll: 377,287 + 199,042 - 168,423 - 10,000 = 397,906). No single total revenues printed for business-type, summed. Governmental transfers in 36,267 / out 26,267 net 10,000 (net 10,000 also appears as business transfers). Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (governmental + business-type). Detail: the All Funds budgetary comparison (p9) is recorded; governmental and business-type lines carry their own fund_type. Other local receipts 216,518 mixes both, so it is split by fund type using pp5/7 (governmental 17,476, business-type 199,042; split_from, computed, review). Transfers in/out are printed below the totals (outside_printed_total); transfers out (36,267) is split 26,267 governmental / 10,000 business-type. Budget amounts of split lines are not split (null). Statement of cash flows (p8) not used since the basis is modified cash (proprietary field null). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
